    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_cd3f9d0f0edb8cee41c033bd4d7a373dea14f77de8e7d69d080550053610e3f8",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Across the six sections, the same all-zeros-on-the-critical-line condition is re-encoded as equality or vanishing of zero counts, square-root-scale prime and arithmetic error, positivity of every test or coefficient, density or completeness in specified function spaces, and determinant conditions for every matrix size. The joint result is an atlas of observables with different information and quantifier structures, not a common proof mechanism linking the criteria.",
